WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.926
DeepSeek ships under an MIT licence.

2
00:00:03.206 --> 00:00:06.550
The licence is open source. The model isn't.

3
00:00:06.829 --> 00:00:07.758
- How does that work?

4
00:00:08.038 --> 00:00:13.889
A licence covers what they gave you. And they gave you a block of numbers.

5
00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:21.182
Weights, settled during training. The brain. And the licence made it sound like the blueprint.

6
00:00:21.462 --> 00:00:29.403
A brain is a lot. Open weight means you run it on your own machines and never call anyone's server again.

7
00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:37.578
Fine-tune it, shrink it onto a laptop, lock it inside your own building. Nobody can switch it off on you.

8
00:00:37.858 --> 00:00:39.158
- So what did they keep?

9
00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:45.661
The data it read, the pipeline that trained it, the code that cleaned the data first.

10
00:00:45.941 --> 00:00:47.566
- So, the cake but not the recipe.

11
00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:54.349
Precisely. Qwen, to its credit, calls its own releases open weight. The honest word for all three.

12
00:00:54.628 --> 00:00:55.882
- It's free though, right?

13
00:00:56.162 --> 00:01:05.636
Read the licence. Llama's has a number in it. Seven hundred million monthly users, and past that you ask Meta for permission.

14
00:01:05.916 --> 00:01:09.631
Meta can say no. That is not what open has ever meant.

15
00:01:09.911 --> 00:01:21.614
Real open source puts four things on the table. The weights, the code that trained it, the architecture, and enough about the data to build it again.

16
00:01:21.894 --> 00:01:22.776
- Anyone could?

17
00:01:23.056 --> 00:01:31.555
Anyone with millions of dollars of computing power. But the drawings are there, and that is the difference.

18
00:01:31.835 --> 00:01:46.928
Even the referees disagree. The Open Source Initiative's 2024 definition doesn't demand the data itself, only a description good enough to rebuild from. Not everyone accepted that.

19
00:01:47.208 --> 00:01:57.936
So when a company says open source, don't look for the download button. Count what's on the table. Anything less than four is open weight.

20
00:01:58.215 --> 00:02:07.085
Open weight gives you the brain. Open source gives you the blueprint as well. Comment WEIGHTS and I'll send the five questions.
